diff --git a/src/config/README.md b/src/config/README.md
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/config/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# Settings
+
+Every value you might tweak to change how the game plays: controls, speeds, distances, timings. The
+game's own addresses and facts are in `../game.h`; menu and HUD positions are in `../../patch_exe.py`
+(`LAYOUT`); `.env` configures the build, not the game.
+
+One file per mode, plus one for what every mode shares:
+
+| File | What |
+|---|---|
+| `foot.h` | On foot: controls, walking and running, jumping and falling, the follow camera, a fare walking with you |
+| `drive.h` | Driving and the cars you take: getting out and in, taking a car, hailing a taxi, the chase camera for taken cars, cars' boxes |
+| `debug.h` | Debugging only, off in a release: the quick start straight into an Arcade run |
+| `world.h` | Shared by every mode: people dodging and storming off, set objects you push, passers-by flying |
+
+Rules:
+
+* A value goes in the file of the mode that uses it; one used by two or more modes goes in `world.h`.
+* A new mode gets its own file.
+* Each value is a named `#define` with a one-line comment: what it is, its unit when not obvious.
+* Code never writes a tunable as a bare number: it names one from here. Maths constants (0, 1, 0.5
+  for a half) stay in the code.
+* The split changes only when growth shows it is needed.
